Context:
I already have a working Stock Analysis & Trade Tracking application.

Requirement:
Add a new feature module called "Momentum Score Dashboard" to the existing application.

Objective:
I want to upload a CSV file containing stock momentum score data. The system should store momentum scores date-wise and generate reports to identify stocks whose momentum score:

- is increasing every day
- score is greater than 60
- supports filtering by:
  - selected date range
  - last 3 days
  - last N days

New Module:
Momentum Score Dashboard

CSV Input Details:

The uploaded CSV may contain these columns:
- Stock Name
- Symbol
- Exch
- Sector Name
- Industry Name
- Score
- 4 Day Change
- Close
- Chg%
- Symbol with Comma for External Upload

However, only consider and store these fields:
- Stock Name
- Symbol
- Sector Name
- Score
- Upload Date/Time

Important:
- Ignore all other CSV columns
- Upload date/time should be captured automatically when CSV is uploaded
- Do not depend on score_date inside CSV
- User may optionally select score date from UI before upload
- If no date selected, use current upload date/time

Functional Requirements:

1. CSV Upload Screen
Create a frontend screen for Momentum Score CSV upload.
Features:
- CSV file upload
- Optional score date picker
- Upload button
- Download sample CSV button
- Upload summary/result section
2. CSV Processing Rules
Supported CSV columns:
- Stock Name
- Symbol
- Sector Name
- Score
Validation Rules:
- Symbol is required
- Stock Name is required
- Score is required
- Score must be numeric
- Score should be stored as decimal/float
- Symbol should be stored in uppercase
- Trim extra spaces
- Skip blank rows
- Ignore unsupported columns
- Reject duplicate rows within same upload

Instruction: Build the backend API and front end and  Updated CLAUDE.md and a new dated entry in docs/ with what changed and why.